# Morning flyers — the light is the imagination (HARD — Founder Nov 28, 2026)

The picture is a world you walk into. Jewel fire, dripping color, one giant idea. Not a style slot. Not a snowy street with a prop in it.

Bar: `assets/_look/december-2026/v14-01-mon-dec21.jpg` (**The light's coming back.**) Same family: Save a wick (`v10-02-sun-dec13.jpg`).

Da Vinci, Einstein, Magritte, Folk, surprise, Oct bank — paint with this imagination. They are not the picture. Einstein is not a chalkboard. Da Vinci is not a sketch of the shop.

## The day is in the picture

Cleopatra doing Tai Chi. Save a wick on candle day. The light on solstice. The object is what that day actually is.

Robert is **Cards**, not tarot. Melissa is **Shaman · Medium**.

## Construction

- One giant thought filling the frame
- Saturated jewel light (coral, magenta, teal, gold) — walk into it
- Dark enough that white type sits on a dark band, not on the flame
- Each day a **different world** — do not repeat the last composition
- Footer still cream: website + phone. Type on the photo, large

## BAN

- Snowy suburban street + giant object + coral/teal sky (Stonehenge in the park, house of cards in the street, runes in the cul-de-sac)
- Factory Magritte / Einstein chalkboard / Da Vinci shop sketch as the idea
- Three days that look like cousins
- Generic mystic dump, glowing healing hands, Flower of Life, tarot Death
- Headline on the bright fire / busy color so you cannot read it

## Mute test

Mute the plate. If a stranger cannot name the punch in one glance, it fails. Do not ship.
